nity\nStudent Life\nOverview\nStudent Awards\nFinancial Support\nStudent Clubs/Interest Groups\nSTUDENT SUPPORT AND WELLBEING\nSocial Good and Excellence\nCentre for Computing for Social Good and Philanthropy (CCSGP)\nCentre for Nurturing Computing Excellence (CENCE)\nOur Heritage\nNUS Computing Gallery\nResearch\nResearch\nOverview\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nResearch Partnership\nResearch Highlights\nKnowledge@Computing\nResearch Bulletin 2025\nResearch Prize\nNUS Computing Ascent Prize Awards\nEntrepreneurship\nInnovation and Entrepreneurship\nOverview\nLeadership\nInnovation\nFunding Opportunities\nAlumni Companies\nNews\nAwards & Competitions\nVenture Initiation Programme@NUSComputing\nNUS Computing Innovation Prize\nAsian Business Plan Competition\nThe Furnace\nOverview\nStart-ups\nIndustry\nIndustry Relations\nOverview\nIndustryConnect (iConnect)\nCareer Fair\nCareer Services\nInternships\nOverview\nFor Employers\nFor Students\nGiving\nNurturing Computing Talent\nMedals and Prizes\nSupporting Student Development\nBursaries and Financial Aid\nScholarships (Merit-based)\nProfessorships\nSpearheading Research\nSearch\nSearch\nMenu\nHome \u00bb Programmes \u00bb Graduate \u00bb Admission Requirements\nPhD (by Research): Admission Requirements\nIntroduction\nEligibility for Application\nOther Admission Requirements\nImportant: The University has not engaged any external agencies to undertake graduate student recruitment on its behalf. Candidates interested in our graduate programmes are advised to apply directly to the University and not through any agents. Candidates who apply through agents will not have any added advantage in gaining admission and the University reserves the right to reject such applications without giving reasons.\nIntroduction\nDoctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) is a research-based programme and is available in the following departments in the School of Computing:\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Information Systems\nEligibility for Application\nThe normal minimum entry qualifications for admission to the programme by research are a good relevant bachelor\u2019s degree/master\u2019s degree. Candidates applying for Research Scholarships must have obtained a bachelor\u2019s degree with at least a 2nd Class Upper Honours, or its equivalent in Computing or related discipline. Candidates should have the ability to pursue research in the candidate\u2019s proposed field of advanced study.\nOther Admission Requirements\nTOEFL/ IELTS\nInternational applicants* are to submit TOEFL/ IELTS test scores as evidence which demonstrates their academic language ability and readiness for graduate study. Candidates may be required to sit for other tests as prescribed by the School.\nGRE\nGRE is not required, but applicants are encouraged to submit their GRE scores. Candidates who have graduated from Indian universities may submit GATE scores instead.\nThe minimum TOEFL scores for Internet Based Test (IBT) is 90; or IELTS score of 6.0. GRE and TOEFL scores will be valid for 5 years and 2 years respectively.\n*International applicants who graduated from universities where English is not the main medium of communication must submit TOEFL (http://www.ets.org/) or IELTS (International English Language Testing System) (http://www.ielts.org) scores.\nSubmission of Test Scores\nApplicants can either:\nsubmit scoresheets certified by Universities with an original stamp; or\nrequest the NUS Department to certify their scoresheets if they are in Singapore; or\nrequest Educational Testing Services (ETS) to send original TOEFL and GRE scores to NUS.\nOverseas Interview\nThe University will conduct overseas interviews for foreign students who have applied for the Research Scholarships. These interviews will be held in mid-March (for the August intake) and mid-August (for January intake). Applicants will be notified of the date, time and venue of the interviews in advance. Applicants should inform the University of any change in their postal addresses.\nReferee's Reports\nRecommendations from two academic referees are required for the application. Please use the referee report forms available online If referees are submitting hardcopy letter, it should be duly signed and place in a sealed envelope whos openings bear their signature.\nClick here for PhD Online Application.\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTelegram\nLinkedin\nYoutube\nSupport NUS Computing\nComputing 1\n13 Computing Drive\nSingapore 117417\n+65 6516 2727\nContact Us\nLocate Us\nFind Our Venues\nAdditional Links\nNUS COMPUTING\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nADMISSIONS\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nRESEARCH\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nDEPARTMENTS\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Information Systems and Analytics\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Information Systems and Analytics\nRESOURCES\nSchool Directory\nStudent Portal\nFacilities & Services\nNUS WebMail\nNUS Canvas\nStudent Jobs\nSchool Directory\nStudent Portal\nFacilities & Services\nNUS WebMail\nNUS Canvas\nStudent Jobs\nNUS COMPUTING\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nAbout Us\nProgrammes\nNews\nEvents\nInnovation & Entrepreneurship\nRecruiters\nProgrammes\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nUndergraduate\nMaster\u2019s\nDoctoral\nGraduate Certificates\nExecutive Education\nADMISSIONS\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFinancial Support\nRESEARCH\nResearch Initiatives\nResearch Areas\nResearch Initiatives\nR